{
  "abstract": "The exceptional regular-twin quintuple with anchor product $-3/4$ has a rational parameter surface carrying all ten pairwise square roots. Extending one of its regular quadruples by its nonzero regular fifth leaves one additional square condition for a sextuple. We determine the canonical model of the resulting marked surface, retaining the original roots. An explicit bidegree-$(8,8)$ branch polynomial has eight rational singular points and two conjugate quadruple points. Blowing up the latter gives a degree-six del Pezzo surface $Y$ with strict branch in $|-4K_Y|$. The double cover has exactly eight $A_5$ and four $A_1$ singularities, so its canonical divisor is the pullback of $-K_Y$. Its smooth minimal model has $K^2=12$, $p_g=7$, $q=0$ and $\\chi=8$, and the canonical map has degree two onto $Y\\subset\\mathbb P^6$. Consequently this marked sextuple source is of general type and admits no rational or elliptic fibration. We also show that every rational fibre of the three conic pencils on $Y$ either has genus three on the cover or forces a zero or repeated entry. Exact Jacobian elimination, boundary gcds, complete-polynomial local calculations and an independent adjoint count certify the result. A published rational sextuple calibrates the nonempty admissible chart. The result does not exclude special low-genus curves, sporadic rational points, arbitrary sixth entries or rational septuples; no birational assertion is made about quotients that forget root witnesses.",
